## URL Param Protocol

All cross-links carry context params so the destination pre-filters:

```
?client_id=blue-coast        — pre-filter to this client
?strategy_id=BTC_BASIS_V3    — pre-filter to this strategy
?venue=binance               — pre-filter to this venue
?component=funding           — pre-filter P&L to this component
?as_of=2026-03-14T14:32:00Z  — point-in-time snapshot (omitted = live)
?period=1w                   — time series period (1d, 1w, 1m, 3m, 1y)
?from=trading                — breadcrumb knows where user came from
```

### Building Cross-Links

```tsx
import { buildCrossLink } from "@unified-trading/ui-kit";

// From Trading Command Center → Market Intelligence P&L
const url = buildCrossLink("marketIntelligence", "/pnl", {
  client_id: "blue-coast",
  strategy_id: "BTC_BASIS_V3",
  from: "trading"
});
// → http://localhost:5180/pnl?client_id=blue-coast&strategy_id=BTC_BASIS_V3&from=trading
```

### Reading Cross-Link Params (receiving side)

```tsx
import { useDeepLinkParams } from "@unified-trading/ui-kit";

function PnLPage() {
  const { clientId, strategyId, from } = useDeepLinkParams();
  // Auto-apply as default filters on mount
}
```

## Surface Registry

Port resolution uses `ui-api-mapping.json` as SSOT. In production, ports become path prefixes.

```tsx
import { SURFACES } from "@unified-trading/ui-kit";

SURFACES.trading          // { name: "Trading", port: 5177 }
SURFACES.strategyAnalytics // { name: "Strategy Analytics", port: 5175 }
SURFACES.marketIntelligence // { name: "Market Intelligence", port: 5180 }
SURFACES.operations        // { name: "Operations", port: 5183 }
SURFACES.config            // { name: "Config", port: 5173 }
SURFACES.mlPlatform        // { name: "ML Platform", port: 5179 }
SURFACES.reporting         // { name: "Reporting", port: 5182 }
```

## Lifecycle Rail → Surface Mapping

| Lifecycle Step | Target Surface | Route |
|---|---|---|
| Design | Config & Onboarding | `/strategies` |
| Simulate | Strategy Analytics | `/grid` |
| Promote | Strategy Analytics | `/grid` (selection + promote flow) |
| Run | Trading Command Center | `/` |
| Monitor | Trading Command Center | `/alerts` |
| Explain | Market Intelligence | `/pnl` |
| Reconcile | Market Intelligence | `/recon` |

## DO

- Use `<EntityLink>` for every entity name in every table cell
- Pass `?from=` so breadcrumbs show navigation history
- Carry filter context across surfaces (client_id, strategy_id)
- Use `buildCrossLink()` — never hardcode URLs or port numbers

## NEVER

- Hardcode `http://localhost:5175` — use SurfaceRegistry
- Navigate to another surface without passing context params
- Duplicate a view instead of cross-linking to the canonical owner
- Build inline navigation that bypasses the GlobalNavBar

